            <ArticleTitle>Thromboembolic complications in coronary angiography. Prevention with acetyl-salicylic acid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>555-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of acetyl-salicylic acid to prevent thromboembolic complications in coronary angiography is reported. No significant difference in fatality rate between the period without and the period with acetyl-salicylic acid was found but significantly less cerebral emboli when acetyl-salicylic acid was given prophylactically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
